00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.620
The EOC is the nerve center of the community's emergency operations.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:43.600
Radiological service is an essential staff function in this and every government EOC.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:52.960
This is where information on the radiological hazard is received, evaluated, analyzed, and put into usable form.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.390
Such information is essential for the conduct of emergency operations.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.460
The assistant RADIF officer is Howard Swanson.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.820
His training has been as intensive as Carter's.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.940
He is fully prepared to assume Carter's job if necessary.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:16.790
George Scully and Fred Morgan are the RAIDF section's plotter analysts.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:22.150
a job which calls for the careful collection and recording of the large volume of RAIDF data

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.740
that will soon come pouring into this EOC.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.990
they will record incoming data on maps and

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.280
