00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.600
They will evaluate radiation decay patterns.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.660
and estimate exposures of people.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.240
Scully and Morgan are not just average citizens either.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.300
They know these procedures as a result of hours of on-the-job training.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.620
The tools of their trade include maps,

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:52.750
overlays,

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:53.560
Slide rules.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.180
Nomograms, graph paper, wax pencils, compasses, protractors.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.460
and fallout templates.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:09.420
In this community, the functions of the RAIDF officer, his assistant, the plotter analyst, are handled by separate people.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.890
However, in smaller government EOCs,

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:18.450
All of the RAIDF activities may have to be combined and handled by one person.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.900
In this EOC, the RAID-F staff is divided into two shifts.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.510
Carter and Scully will handle one shift.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.140
Swanson and Morgan the other.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:36.580
One of the initial activities will be forecasting fallout based on the UF wind data.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:38.250
and likely target areas.

