00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:20.640
Dan Carter will provide the emergency information officer with information to be included in an advisory which will be broadcast over the local area emergency broadcast system station.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:26.890
These advisories will tell the public what will probably happen.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:29.970
how it will affect them, and what steps they should take.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.920
to protect themselves.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:38.340
These advisories are also of value to industries with extensive shutdown operations.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:46.660
and to farmers and ranchers in making arrangements for the protection of their livestock as well as their families.

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:51.140
The forecasts, however, are only rough predictions.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:59.990
The actual fallout arrival time can only be determined by trained monitors at fixed

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.450
field locations and in public shelters periodically check outside radiation

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:14.560
level when the radiation level reaches five tenths of a rent can per hour

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:18.820
Monitors send flash reports of fallout arrival to the EOC.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:29.950
As EOC's downwind of Cobb Air Force Base verify the arrival of fallout, this information is fed...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.660
into both state and neighboring EOCs.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:34.820
as well as into Dan Carter's section.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:38.020
This mutual exchange of RADEF information

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:44.810
verifies forecasts and other radiological information being plotted by similar staffs in other EOCs.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:58.880
Following the flash report, the RADF monitor will provide an unsheltered dose rate report to his EOC at least once each three hours for the first 24 hours.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:07:59.980
They're out.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.960
